enter of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98792725-41a0-5da0-b5d6-db129288946a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283232} {:answer/id #uuid "85fa5698-91ef-5c47-ba6f-ce806d63abad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98792725-41a0-5da0-b5d6-db129288946a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283232} :answer-field/id #uuid "a46e7f45-4f14-549b-8d34-2661338a50d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1591d5c8-2a19-5ea4-9ff8-fe4dff361aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1591d5c8-2a19-5ea4-9ff8-fe4dff361aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283235} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aeef4ab-8348-5c3d-8693-991a60de3e78" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9b14a36-f374-5fea-92c5-1f777c17e46a" :question/math-academy-id "q-328355" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+6y=11$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+6y & =11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)-({y}^{2}-6y) & =11 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]-[(y-3)^{2}-9] & =11 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4-(y-3)^{2}+9 & =11 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-3)^{2} & =11+4-9 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3/2}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,3\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72c86939-8c99-5a56-8ffe-383a1b611c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291473} {:answer/id #uuid "f5884a66-2e21-5b66-bcf5-af8f60d4b733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72c86939-8c99-5a56-8ffe-383a1b611c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291473} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc4a7150-b28b-5f86-bf16-b80258a5f170" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baf47612-0907-5263-95fe-e164d900bd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baf47612-0907-5263-95fe-e164d900bd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291476} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd4b86e-2a1b-5c6a-86a9-1e03505a534b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de9dda81-a345-5236-acbb-5d210b78c08c" :question/math-academy-id "q-328358" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y=7$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y & =7 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)-({y}^{2}-2y) & =7 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]-[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4-(y-1)^{2}+1 & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =7+4-1 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5/2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,1\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ddd94d-90a0-53e3-8abb-b11acbe51e9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7, 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082437} {:answer/id #uuid "a97c4262-c284-5fde-b161-07cc979c4857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082438} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca93485-fe8d-5c89-bfc6-22089a5f9947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082439} {:answer/id #uuid "334e5cc5-b7dc-5a1e-b76b-b82fc9f0449d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082440} {:answer/id #uuid "66baaf99-5bbe-5603-acdf-75b5b2a2d875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "334e5cc5-b7dc-5a1e-b76b-b82fc9f0449d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082440} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb98a281-906c-5c0c-8750-ea5f0e7d4df2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082436}] :question/id #uuid "ecad8073-32a5-5bcd-a4f6-4e37160bc7af" :question/math-academy-id "q-78254" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $((x + 4)^{2})/(7) - ((y - 2)^{2})/(6) = 1$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "497cdc95-c50d-5298-baba-6d1ae1802e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264060} {:answer/id #uuid "0c9aa5c6-04aa-5dc6-a6f3-34b0fd557dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264061} {:answer/id #uuid "478c00d4-b26e-5865-a66d-153e3da485c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264062} {:answer/id #uuid "46662acd-00cb-5cdc-8797-d45261ea0904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264063} {:answer/id #uuid "3b179b00-2c55-5cb5-acb2-7fe6996cfe22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "478c00d4-b26e-5865-a66d-153e3da485c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264062} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e4b4ad-d430-5d15-9844-b414a6cf495a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0757e929-9428-56e6-9794-2fa909206184" :question/math-academy-id "q-78379" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y=12?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y & =12 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-12y-3{x}^{2}+12x & =12 \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}-6y]-3[{x}^{2}-4x] & =12 \\\\ 2[(y-3)^{2}-9]-3[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-18-3(x-2)^{2}+12 & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =12+18-12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e157b772-ba84-50df-baba-164296320193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264067} {:answer/id #uuid "1ab443f0-106f-50b8-809a-4a4f0acb65fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264068} {:answer/id #uuid "06ca6a2e-4455-5322-8752-4cfea94c0157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264069} {:answer/id #uuid "a688d7fa-c6ce-5c93-9778-8e520508e6a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264070} {:answer/id #uuid "23438b5f-9721-5273-94c5-d8a247c141c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06ca6a2e-4455-5322-8752-4cfea94c0157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264069} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b9f66f0-12f1-5ace-a8f3-d476e4f05cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45f8a767-fd63-5ed1-aa77-8691f5b484a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-78860" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=0$ and $k=3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(0,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7318ed52-b5d6-52a1-a771-333d18578307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292907} {:answer/id #uuid "ae6df21f-943c-5bda-a647-56b849766d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292908} {:answer/id #uuid "3e9e4df3-52af-5a57-9f44-011e417573b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292909} {:answer/id #uuid "6364d58e-2fd4-5f1f-877f-5b3230936160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292910} {:answer/id #uuid "82ea2dc5-4aed-5797-8435-8c74b31f1e50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6364d58e-2fd4-5f1f-877f-5b3230936160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292910} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6b5fcd-1080-5de0-9c6e-99bbcb2f126d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2096e13-b432-5188-9b2a-286612b8e650" :question/math-academy-id "q-78868" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-(x+4)^{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{1}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-4$ and $k=7.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-4,7).$"}]}
